---
export const title = "Serial Experiments Lain Fanart/Study";
export const date = "2026-10-25";
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import lain from "../../assets/gallery/art-lain.png";
import lainsketch from "../../assets/gallery/artlog-lain-sketch.jpg";
import lainprogress1 from "../../assets/gallery/artlog-lain-progress1.jpg";
import lainprogress2 from "../../assets/gallery/artlog-lain-progress2.jpg";
---

<BlogLayout title={title} date={date}>

  <Image
    src={lain}
    alt="Serial Experiments Lain Fanart"
    style="width: 100%; max-width: 600px; height: auto;"
  />

  <p>
    This is actually a study of a cool piece I found on pinterest by Pablo
    Uchida. I wanted to practice painting and freeing my characters from the
    white void I always draw them in.
  </p>

  <img
    src="https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcR_BJR02IcV1MFjlTgseAnH-0ladk8NbhoyYOFP44Skw6x0sCqbkgnQrIw&s=10"
    width="600px"
  />

  <p>
    I started off with some sketches. You can see me try and give up on coming
    up with my own composition.
  </p>

  <Image
    src={lainsketch}
    alt="Serial Experiments Lain Fanart"
    style="width: 100%; max-width: 600px; height: auto;"
  />

  <p>
    Then to digital! I have some low quality progress pics I took on my phone.
  </p>

  <Image
    src={lainprogress1}
    alt="Serial Experiments Lain Fanart"
    style="width: 100%; max-width: 600px; height: auto;"
  />

  <Image
    src={lainprogress2}
    alt="Serial Experiments Lain Fanart"
    style="width: 100%; max-width: 600px; height: auto;"
  />

  <p>
    Final piece! I was feeling kind of good about it toward the end 
    but then I looked at my reference again and realised how much it 
    mogs mine. I still have a long way to go...
  </p>

  <Image
    src={lain}
    alt="Serial Experiments Lain Fanart"
    style="width: 100%; max-width: 600px; height: auto;"
  />

</BlogLayout>
